# ============================================================
# Journal_Notion / Life Calendar — .gitignore
# ============================================================
# This is a PERSONAL journal pipeline. The single most important
# rule: never commit the journal contents, the scored data, the
# generated dashboards, or any API credentials. Treat everything
# derived from your entries as private by default.
# ============================================================

# ---------- SECRETS / CREDENTIALS (highest priority) ----------
notion_token.txt
openai_key.txt
*_key.txt
*_token.txt
.Renviron
.env
.env.*
# The shared API-keys folder referenced by the LLM pass
00.APIKeys/

# ---------- PRIVATE DATA (your journal — never commit) ----------
# Source-of-truth workbook and all its variants
Output/journal_enriched.xlsx
Output/journal_LLM_context.csv
Output/*.xlsx
Output/*.csv
Output/*.json
Output/*.png
Output/*.html
0x_Timelines.R
0x1_SQuad.R

# Generated dashboards (contain full entry text)
life_dashboard.html
life_dashboard_demo.html
Output/Life_Timeline.html
Output/timeline_data.json

# Any stray data drops
Data/
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
!**/templates/*.xlsx      # (allow template stubs if you ever add them)

# ---------- R ----------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj.bak

# ---------- Python / venv ----------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# nbconvert scratch output
*.nbconvert.py

# ---------- Editor / OS ----------
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------- Explicitly KEEP (whitelist the code) ----------
# Scripts, templates, and docs are safe to track. They are not
# ignored above, but listed here for clarity of intent:
#   Scripts/*.R
#   Scripts/*.ipynb
#   Scripts/03.5_Calendar_base.html
#   Scripts/timeline_template.html
#   README.md
